@verbs channels channel emergency guild clan race adventurer
@tier player
@title channels: talking to a group wherever they are
@see say nickname party

A channel carries what you write to everybody listening to it, no
matter where you all are. Each channel is a verb of its own:

  emergency    open to every player, to ask for help.
  guild        for the members of your guild.
  clan         for the members of your clan.
  race         for those of your own racial group.
  adventurer   for the party you are adventuring with.

The three in the middle only work if you belong to that guild, clan
or racial group, and if the group has a channel of its own.

Typing the channel name and nothing else does nothing; it needs
something to say:

  <channel> <message>   sends it to whoever is listening.
  <channel> ?           reminds you of these options.
  <channel> !           repeats the last twenty messages.
  <channel> off         stops listening to it.
  <channel> on          listens again.

A channel you turned off will not let you talk on it either. The
adventurer one is the exception: it opens and closes by itself as
you join and leave a party, and takes neither 'on' nor 'off'.
